@startuml embed-vectorstore-workflow

title Embed - Embedding, Indexing & RAG Vector Store Integration

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left

start

:Receive NormalizedTextDocument,\nRAGChunkSet, TrustMetrics\n(from Chunk);

:Determine target collection /\nindex and namespace\n(based on project/app config);

partition "Chunk filtering & routing" {
  :Filter or down-weight chunks\nwith low trust_score or\nhigh hallucination_risk\n(if policy requires);

  :Optionally split or merge\nchunks for app-specific\nsize constraints;
}

partition "Embedding generation" {
  :Select embedding model\nbased on:\n- document domain/type\n- multilingual needs\n- model policy;

  :Generate embeddings for\naccepted chunks\n(batch processing);

  :Attach embedding metadata:\n- chunk_id\n- document_id\n- page_range\n- section hierarchy\n- trust scores\n- OCR engine provenance;
}

partition "Vector store operations" {
  :Write embeddings + metadata\ninto configured vector DB\n(e.g., pgvector, Milvus,\nWeaviate, etc.);

  :Update any secondary indices\n(e.g., keyword index,\nsection-level catalog);

  :Record ingestion statistics\nfor monitoring:\n#chunks, avg trust,\npages processed;
}

:Emit ingestion result:\n- collection / index ID\n- document handle\n- summary statistics;

stop

note right
  **CONTEXT DIAGRAM**
  This diagram shows the downstream Embed project's workflow.
  It is provided here to illustrate how Prepare-Doc quality
  provenance flows through to vector store metadata.
  Embed internals are NOT part of the Prepare-Doc codebase.

  **Prepare-Doc Outputs Consumed (via Unify + Chunk):**
  - Trust scores derived from Prepare-Doc IQA metrics
  - OCR engine provenance rooted in Prepare-Doc routing

  **Documentation:**
  [[docs/development/RAG Pipeline/RAG-pipeline-project-overview.md]]
  [[docs/architecture/diagrams/level-2/downstream-context/index.md]]

  **ADR:**
  [[docs/ADRs/0029-prepare-doc-scope-boundaries.md]]
end note

@enduml
